<title>USA: U.S. appeals court stays Lloyd's injunction.</title>
<headline>U.S. appeals court stays Lloyd's injunction.</headline>
<dateline>BALTIMORE 1996-08-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>A U.S. appeals court ruled Tuesday in favor of Lloyd's of London, granting the insurance syndicate a last-minute reprieve from an injunction that Lloyd's said put its $22 billion reorganization plan in jeopardy.</p>
<p>The three-judge panel sent the case back to the district court with instructions to dismiss it.</p>
</text>
